A weathered blacksmith's forge in warm amber light, rendered in Vincent van Gogh's expressive brushstroke style with swirling textures and bold impasto. In the foreground, rough hands guide younger hands shaping glowing orange metal on an anvil. Sparks dance upward in spiraling patterns reminiscent of Starry Night. Tools hang on wooden walls—hammers, tongs, files—each showing years of use. A half-finished decorative iron piece sits cooling nearby, showing the progression from raw material to craftsmanship. Deep blues and vibrant oranges dominate the palette, with visible directional brushstrokes creating movement and energy throughout the scene. The composition conveys knowledge transfer, tradition, and the sacred passing of skills between generations.
